7592186045417] [17592186525330 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525330 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32717fe3-a7f3-56f5-9f8f-5f4636b81c3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525401 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525401 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525401 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d91a2bf-fdbf-56b8-8e4e-20e5996d747e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525527 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525527 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525527 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "80bb61ff-4612-53a2-9ac0-e8606aaa9455" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525611 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525611 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525611 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ef395c5-e379-5f31-abfb-14bad75b8656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186525269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7be66281-82ba-5671-8686-d76669d37ebe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-178268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$\n\nII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})\\}$ is orthogonal\n\nIII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})\\}$ is orthonormal" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01fe6b4b-89e7-5f7d-85f4-05ba3856f335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525984 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2+2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that, $Q({u}_{1})⊥̸Q({u}_{2})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{2})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since the set is not even orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526116 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186526134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526116 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4d191177-8534-5319-9822-9c254342b4c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526116 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526134 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186526152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526134 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9d7f5e67-89e2-5703-a73e-0cdea17e3e7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526134 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526141 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186526116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526141 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c40cc94f-25ae-53ce-9f12-3dc6d6e1c8c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526141 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526149 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e78e4d3a-6a64-53a3-9a97-006207c74a48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526149 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186284764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526152 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186526149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526152 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eef50253-8c08-55c7-bab7-bc37bdee6bfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526152 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186525984 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
